{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And the Fear of Yitzchak.</b> He did not want to say 'Elohei Yitzchak,' for the Holy One, blessed be He, does not unify His name upon the righteous in their lifetime. And even though He said to him when he left Be'er Sheva, ״אָנֹכִי יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם אָבִיךָ וֵאלֹהֵי יִצְחָק,״ that was because his eyes had grown dim, and he was like one dead. Ya'akov was afraid to say 'Elohei,' so he said 'and the Fear of.'" "<b>And He will reprove.</b> It is a term of תּוֹכָחָה and not a term of הוֹכָחָה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:36.411649197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}